From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zerollama <zerollama@local>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 01:41:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cuda: add QJL/Polar/TBQ CUDA kernels
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Copy CUDA kernel files from elizaOS fork:
  qjl.cu/.cuh         — QJL 1-bit score kernel (warp-level popcnt)
  qjl-set-rows.cuh    — QJL SET_ROWS (quantize-on-write to K-cache)
  polarquant.cu/.cuh  — PolarQuant Q4 decode + dot (Hadamard in shared mem)
  polar-set-rows.cuh  — PolarQuant SET_ROWS
  turbo-tcq.cu/.cuh   — TBQ3_TCQ 9-bit codebook decode kernel
  turbo-tcq-codebook.h — TCQ codebook LUT for CUDA constant memory
  turboquant.cuh      — TBQ3/4 dequant shared utility
  fused-attn.cu/.cuh  — fused attention dispatch (score + softmax + V-mix)
  fused-attn-qjl-tbq.cu  — fused QJL-K + TBQ-V attention kernel
  fused-attn-qjl-polar.cu — fused QJL-K + Polar-V attention kernel
  template-instances/fattn-vec-instance-tbq*.cu — flash-attn vec TBQ combos

Wire CMakeLists.txt options (all default ON except fused-attn which is OFF):
  GGML_CUDA_QJL, GGML_CUDA_POLARQUANT, GGML_CUDA_TBQ3_TCQ,
  GGML_CUDA_FUSED_ATTN_QJL

Kernel bodies are gated by #ifdef so they compile to empty stubs when
the option is OFF. The existing file(GLOB *.cu) already picks up new
files; fattn TBQ instances added via explicit glob.
